<title>SPAIN: Spain's investment in Cuba rose sharply in 1996.</title>
<headline>Spain's investment in Cuba rose sharply in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's direct investment in Cuba rose sharply in the first nine months of 1996 to 1.43 billion pesetas from 527 million in the same period a year earlier, data from the Economy Ministry showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Spanish investment in Cuba represents only 0.19 percent of Spain's total direct foreign investment.</p>
<p>But it has risen sharply in the last two years. In 1994, Spain had no direct investment in the island.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
